Happy early birthday to your husband! Here is what I found for Friday 11 September.

**Availability**
- The Warehouse tasting tour runs at 14:30 and has 11 places left, so there is room for the two of you. It is for ages 18 and over.
- The only other tour that day is the Classic tour at 11:00, which has 4 places.

**Accessibility**
- The shop, cafe and still house are step-free and have a lift.
- The warehouse floor is uneven. I don't have more detail than that, such as how uneven it is or whether there is an alternative route for wheelchair users. Since the warehouse is the main part of the tasting tour, I'd suggest contacting the visitor centre before you book so they can tell you whether it will work for your husband.

**Parking**
- There is free parking for cars beside the visitor centre. I don't have details of specific accessible bays or which space is closest to the entrance, so it's worth asking about that when you speak to the team.

I can also check the opening and cafe hours if you'd like to have lunch before the tour.
